WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.3 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Indicators

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
An indicator is a clear sign that a result is happening, measured the same way by everyone.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
An indicator is a specific sign you track to show whether a result is happening. It is defined so clearly that you, a co-founder or the first person who joins would all measure it the same way.

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
What every indicator records

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:41.944
Definition: The sign you track, with who counts as a success and out of whom. For example: % of trainees who find a job within three months, out of all who finished.

6
00:00:41.944 --> 00:00:52.163
Source and method: Where the data comes from and how you collect it. For example: A follow-up call by the youth-centre mentor three months after the traineeship ends.

7
00:00:52.163 --> 00:01:00.159
Frequency: How often you collect it. For example: Once per group of trainees, three months after the six months end.

8
00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:10.096
Owner: Who collects it and answers for it. For example: The founder who leads trainee support, until a mentor takes it on.

9
00:01:10.496 --> 00:01:11.096
Why it matters

10
00:01:11.096 --> 00:01:16.400
1. It turns a vague hope into something you can check.

11
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.704
2. Everyone measures the same way, so numbers compare over time.

12
00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:28.007
3. Breaking data down shows unequal results from your first group.

13
00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:29.007
What it guides

14
00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:33.941
1. Your baselines and targets, set in the next lesson.

15
00:01:33.941 --> 00:01:39.615
2. Your data collection plan: each indicator needs a source and method.

16
00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:45.548
3. Your monitoring dashboard: planned versus actual for each indicator.

17
00:01:45.948 --> 00:01:46.548
What to avoid

18
00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:50.741
Counting activities, like sessions run, as outcomes.

19
00:01:50.741 --> 00:01:54.933
Percentages without a clear numerator and denominator.

20
00:01:54.933 --> 00:02:01.607
Counting the same person twice, or data you cannot collect ethically.

21
00:02:02.207 --> 00:02:04.007
You write an indicator reference sheet for your priority results.

22
00:02:04.007 --> 00:02:08.007
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:09.507 --> 00:02:12.607
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
